From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] backlight: ktz8869_iceland: do not crash when the second IC
 is removed

The second KTZ8869 ("ktz8869b") only stores itself in ktz_b at probe:
it registers no backlight device and sets no client data. Its remove
callback still takes the client data as a backlight device and
dereferences it, so unbinding the second IC, or unloading the module
with both ICs bound, oopses on a NULL pointer. ktz_b also kept pointing
at the freed device data, which the first IC's writes would then use.

Return early for an IC without a backlight device and clear ktz_b when
it is the one going away.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
index 9d6dde311e58..8930f570fc68 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/ktz8869_iceland.c
@@ -315,6 +315,17 @@ static int ktz8869_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 static void ktz8869_remove(struct i2c_client *client)
 {
 	struct backlight_device *backlight_dev = i2c_get_clientdata(client);
+
+	/*
+	 * The second IC registers no backlight device and sets no client
+	 * data: it only has to stop taking the first IC's writes.
+	 */
+	if (!backlight_dev) {
+		if (ktz_b && ktz_b->client == client)
+			ktz_b = NULL;
+		return;
+	}
+
 	backlight_dev->props.brightness = 0;
 	backlight_update_status(backlight_dev);
 }
